# Cursor Editor — Architecture Overview

## What is Cursor

Cursor is an AI-native code editor built on VSCode with a layered agent architecture. It enables developers to interact with AI through multiple interaction modes and provides a programmable surface for automation via its SDK, MCP integration, skills system, and rules engine.

### Interaction Modes

| Mode | Description | Use Case |
|---|---|---|
| **Agent Mode** | Full autonomy with access to all tools (file ops, shell, LSP, terminal). Can modify code, run commands, and execute complex multi-step tasks. | Implementation, debugging, refactoring, file operations |
| **Ask Mode** | Read-only exploration. Can search, read files, and answer questions but cannot modify the codebase. | Research, code understanding, documentation |
| **Plan Mode** | [Switchable] Collaborative, design-only mode for approaching tasks with complex trade-offs. | Architecture decisions, planning, exploration |

